1
00:00:01,953 --> 00:00:04,117
Answer for what you have done.

2
00:00:04,632 --> 00:00:07,237
Yone, go back.

3
00:00:07,813 --> 00:00:09,798
You have dishonored us.

4
00:00:10,272 --> 00:00:12,617
You swore to protect him.

5
00:00:13,432 --> 00:00:15,876
And you swore to protect Ionia...

6
00:00:16,472 --> 00:00:18,636
Look around you, brother.

7
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:21,416
Your honor stains the earth.

8
00:00:22,073 --> 00:00:23,922
Better than dishonor.

9
00:00:23,952 --> 00:00:25,778
Forgive me, brother.

10
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:28,898
I will never shame you again.

11
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:34,386
Yasuo killed the only person who had protected
him all his life: his own older brother.

12
00:00:34,497 --> 00:00:37,250
But the cruelest part
of this story is this:

13
00:00:37,421 --> 00:00:40,294
he never committed the
murder he was blamed for.

14
00:00:40,405 --> 00:00:44,320
So why would a brother draw
his sword on his own brother?

15
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:50,686
This story begins in a
small village in Ionia.

16
00:00:50,817 --> 00:00:54,032
Yasuo's father left them
before he was even born.

17
00:00:54,103 --> 00:00:57,057
Everyone in the village
saw him as a burden.

18
00:00:57,128 --> 00:00:58,500
Except for one person.

19
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:02,556
Remember what you have lost.

20
00:01:03,892 --> 00:01:05,367
Let me go, Yone!

21
00:01:05,461 --> 00:01:06,862
I was going to win!

22
00:01:06,892 --> 00:01:09,195
Did you see how I was
taking down that big kid?

23
00:01:09,912 --> 00:01:11,996
He was trampling on your honor.

24
00:01:13,783 --> 00:01:14,917
But you also...

25
00:01:15,292 --> 00:01:16,632
I fight when I must.

26
00:01:16,662 --> 00:01:17,977
Not for the fun of it.

27
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:20,760
You have nothing to prove.

28
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:23,864
His older brother Yone
always protected him.

29
00:01:23,894 --> 00:01:27,408
Yasuo was impatient,
fast and hot-tempered.

30
00:01:27,479 --> 00:01:31,695
Yone was calm, composed
and devoted to his duty.

31
00:01:31,725 --> 00:01:36,060
Two opposites, yet two
brothers who were never apart.

32
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,530
At the school, every eye was on Yasuo.

33
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,510
Because Yasuo could feel the wind.

34
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:50,791
The last master of the wind technique, Elder
Souma, chose him as his student and his protector.

35
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:53,151
At first, Yasuo refused.

36
00:01:53,181 --> 00:01:55,431
Once again, it was Yone who convinced him.

37
00:01:55,461 --> 00:02:00,832
He gave his brother a small maple
seed, the school's symbol of humility.

38
00:02:00,862 --> 00:02:03,792
Yasuo took the seed and
learned the technique.

39
00:02:03,822 --> 00:02:07,992
The wind was now his shield,
his sword and his shadow.

40
00:02:08,542 --> 00:02:11,993
The brothers' sparring duels
drew crowds in the village.

41
00:02:12,023 --> 00:02:16,993
But no one knew that one day these
two blades would truly clash.

42
00:02:17,543 --> 00:02:19,353
Then Noxus came.

43
00:02:19,383 --> 00:02:21,833
The empire invaded Ionia.

44
00:02:21,863 --> 00:02:24,693
Villages burned, temples fell.

45
00:02:25,243 --> 00:02:27,420
The students were called to war.

46
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:29,927
But Yasuo was given a single order:

47
00:02:29,957 --> 00:02:32,413
stay here and protect Souma.

48
00:02:32,956 --> 00:02:34,719
Your place is here.

49
00:02:35,498 --> 00:02:36,904
At Master Souma's side.

50
00:02:36,934 --> 00:02:39,320
This is what he trained me for.

51
00:02:39,976 --> 00:02:42,181
With my help, the war could end.

52
00:02:46,316 --> 00:02:48,560
Your duty is to this school.

53
00:02:49,279 --> 00:02:50,316
To your master.

54
00:02:51,178 --> 00:02:52,437
To Ionia.

55
00:02:53,357 --> 00:02:55,561
Then I must go and protect it.

56
00:02:56,916 --> 00:02:59,221
I won't fail you, Yone.

57
00:03:00,882 --> 00:03:03,681
I have already failed you.

58
00:03:04,063 --> 00:03:05,993
But Yasuo could not stay put.

59
00:03:06,023 --> 00:03:09,153
He believed he could turn
the war with his own sword.

60
00:03:09,183 --> 00:03:11,774
He abandoned his post
and ran to the front.

61
00:03:11,804 --> 00:03:14,974
By the time he got there,
the battle was long over.

62
00:03:15,524 --> 00:03:18,554
When he returned to the school, he
found Elder Souma on the ground.

63
00:03:18,584 --> 00:03:20,034
His master was dead.

64
00:03:20,064 --> 00:03:22,814
And what had killed him was the wind.

65
00:03:23,364 --> 00:03:26,354
Yasuo was the only student
who knew the wind technique.

66
00:03:26,384 --> 00:03:27,954
He had abandoned his post.

67
00:03:27,984 --> 00:03:29,874
Every trace led to him.

68
00:03:29,904 --> 00:03:31,734
No one asked what had happened.

69
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:33,254
And Yasuo did not explain.

70
00:03:33,284 --> 00:03:34,284
He ran.

71
00:03:34,784 --> 00:03:37,575
His old schoolmates began to hunt him.

72
00:03:37,605 --> 00:03:40,115
Each time, Yasuo defended himself.

73
00:03:40,145 --> 00:03:43,835
And each time, he buried one more friend.

74
00:03:44,435 --> 00:03:47,383
Brother, what have you become?

75
00:03:47,413 --> 00:03:49,576
If I told you, would you listen?

76
00:03:49,674 --> 00:03:51,784
You committed a crime, you are wanted.

77
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:53,717
I am not a murderer.

78
00:03:53,854 --> 00:03:56,117
Answer for what you have done.

79
00:03:56,617 --> 00:04:00,947
In the end, the one person he expected
but never wanted to face appeared.

80
00:04:00,977 --> 00:04:04,208
Yone, who had come to bring
his brother to justice.

81
00:04:04,758 --> 00:04:07,528
This is the duel you saw
at the start of the story.

82
00:04:07,558 --> 00:04:10,188
The two brothers circled each other.

83
00:04:10,218 --> 00:04:12,228
Their techniques were evenly matched.

84
00:04:12,258 --> 00:04:14,988
But the wind was on Yasuo's side.

85
00:04:15,538 --> 00:04:16,888
Yone fell.

86
00:04:16,918 --> 00:04:20,648
Yasuo dropped to his knees
and begged for forgiveness.

87
00:04:20,678 --> 00:04:25,068
Yone's last words were that Souma
had died by the wind technique.

88
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:26,928
And he died without forgiving him.

89
00:04:27,478 --> 00:04:30,489
Yasuo buried his brother
with his own hands.

90
00:04:30,519 --> 00:04:33,129
Then he took up his sword
and went on his way.

91
00:04:33,159 --> 00:04:37,309
He no longer had a home,
a school, or a brother.

92
00:04:37,859 --> 00:04:40,149
Years later, the truth came out.

93
00:04:40,179 --> 00:04:42,630
It was not Yasuo who killed Souma.

94
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,910
It was a Noxian soldier.

95
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:46,270
Her name was Riven.

96
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:51,390
She had done terrible things against
Ionia in the war, then deserted her army.

97
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:54,950
She wanted to be rid of the
cursed runeblade in her hands.

98
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,011
She came to Souma and begged
him to destroy the sword.

99
00:04:59,041 --> 00:05:02,131
Souma tried to break it
with the wind technique.

100
00:05:02,161 --> 00:05:06,291
The blade shattered, and the
blast killed the old master.

101
00:05:06,841 --> 00:05:11,852
So Yasuo had spilled his brother's
blood over a murder he never committed.

102
00:05:12,402 --> 00:05:16,292
Riven was caught, tried in
the village, and confessed.

103
00:05:16,322 --> 00:05:18,192
That night, Yasuo found her.

104
00:05:18,222 --> 00:05:23,253
He threw the pieces of the broken sword
at her feet and challenged her to a duel.

105
00:05:23,803 --> 00:05:26,893
But by the end of the fight,
they both saw the same thing.

106
00:05:26,923 --> 00:05:29,093
Each of them was carrying their own guilt.

107
00:05:29,123 --> 00:05:31,853
The village elder told Yasuo:

108
00:05:31,943 --> 00:05:35,573
Accepting responsibility is
the first step to atonement.

109
00:05:35,644 --> 00:05:38,074
Forgiving yourself is the second.

110
00:05:38,624 --> 00:05:40,714
Yasuo managed the first step.

111
00:05:40,744 --> 00:05:42,294
He could not take the second.

112
00:05:42,404 --> 00:05:44,014
And once again, he set out on the road.

113
00:05:44,564 --> 00:05:45,954
Years passed.

114
00:05:46,044 --> 00:05:51,455
During the Spirit Blossom Festival, on the night when
the spirits of the dead are closest to the living,

115
00:05:51,485 --> 00:05:53,515
Yasuo arrived at a shrine.

116
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:56,803
Let the waters cleanse you.

117
00:05:59,197 --> 00:06:03,003
Let the current carry
away the burden you bear.

118
00:06:03,265 --> 00:06:05,935
But the woman at the shrine was no guide.

119
00:06:05,965 --> 00:06:07,455
She was an azakana.

120
00:06:07,485 --> 00:06:10,735
A demon that feeds on human guilt.

121
00:06:10,785 --> 00:06:15,876
And Yasuo's guilt was the greatest
feast she could find in all of Ionia.

122
00:06:16,418 --> 00:06:19,924
Sometimes we must seek out our own demons.

123
00:06:28,326 --> 00:06:33,296
When Yasuo fell, a masked swordsman
emerged from the darkness.

124
00:06:33,326 --> 00:06:35,136
Yasuo recognized that technique.

125
00:06:35,166 --> 00:06:39,137
Because it belonged to the man
he had buried with his own hands.

126
00:06:51,687 --> 00:06:53,157
The demon was defeated.

127
00:06:53,207 --> 00:06:57,377
Yasuo laid down his sword
and knelt before his brother.

128
00:06:57,407 --> 00:07:00,537
He waited for the judgment he
had been expecting for years.

129
00:07:01,303 --> 00:07:03,385
Take your revenge, brother.

130
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,784
Maybe you deserve death.

131
00:07:07,164 --> 00:07:09,125
But not by my hand.

132
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:15,145
Then there is nothing
left for me in Ionia.

133
00:07:18,439 --> 00:07:21,365
Even the wind has a path, brother.

134
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,944
Farewell, Yone.

135
00:07:31,921 --> 00:07:35,105
May the spirit of Ionia guide you.

136
00:07:35,287 --> 00:07:38,158
Yone turned his back and
walked into the dark.

137
00:07:38,188 --> 00:07:41,278
He neither killed Yasuo nor forgave him.

138
00:07:41,308 --> 00:07:44,778
Perhaps that was a punishment
heavier than death.

139
00:07:45,328 --> 00:07:47,978
Yasuo left Ionia behind.

140
00:07:48,008 --> 00:07:52,819
But the wind was not carrying him to an empty
road, it was carrying him to a new story.

141
00:07:53,262 --> 00:07:55,686
Looking back is easy, isn't it?

142
00:07:57,402 --> 00:08:00,192
The real challenge is
seeing what is to come.

143
00:08:00,222 --> 00:08:03,107
I think we will find a lot there.

144
00:08:03,369 --> 00:08:06,819
So, if you were him, would
you forgive your brother?
